<h2 id="sec-2">How We Tested</h2>
<p>Every robot vacuum underwent standardized testing in a 1,200 sq ft apartment with mixed flooring. We measured dirt pickup efficiency on hardwood, tile, and low-pile carpet; navigation accuracy and coverage percentage; noise level in decibels; real-world battery runtime; app setup ease and feature availability; and obstacle avoidance around common household items.</p>
<h2 id="sec-3">Top Picks Reviewed</h2>
<h3>1. Roborock Qrevo — Best Overall</h3>
<p>The Roborock Qrevo redefines what you can expect from a sub-$300 robot vacuum. Its 5,000 Pa suction is class-leading, and the LiDAR navigation creates precise maps in under 5 minutes. The self-emptying dock holds up to 60 days of debris, meaning you can set it and forget it for weeks.</p>
<div style="background:#F7F4EF;border-left:3px solid #C9A962;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-size:0.95rem"><strong>Best for:</strong> Homes with mixed flooring, pet owners, and anyone who wants a truly set-it-and-forget-it cleaning experience.</p></div>
<h3>2. Eufy RoboVac X8 — Best Value</h3>
<p>At $249, the Eufy RoboVac X8 delivers remarkable performance. Its 4,000 Pa Twin-Turbine technology provides strong suction, while the iSee+ visual navigation maps your home accurately. The 170-minute battery covers homes up to 2,500 sq ft on a single charge.</p>
<h3>3. Shark IQ Robot — Best for Pet Hair</h3>
<p>Shark's reputation for pet hair removal carries over to the IQ Robot. Its self-emptying base uses AirSense technology to detect when the bin is full and seals it airtight. The Matrix Clean pattern ensures complete coverage systematically.</p>
<h2 id="sec-4">Buying Guide</h2>
<p><strong>Navigation:</strong> LiDAR is the gold standard. Avoid gyroscopic-only models for larger homes. <strong>Suction:</strong> Aim for 2,000+ Pa minimum; 4,000+ handles carpets and pet hair. <strong>Self-emptying:</strong> Worth the extra $50-80 if you have pets.</p>
<h2 id="sec-5">FAQs</h2>
<h3>Do robot vacuums work well on carpets?</h3>
<p>Yes, models with 3,000+ Pa handle low to medium-pile carpets effectively. High-pile carpets remain challenging for all robot vacuums.</p>
<h3>How often do I need to empty the dustbin?</h3>
<p>Without self-emptying, expect every 2-3 cycles. With self-emptying bases, 4-8 weeks between emptying the dock.</p>
